ITEM BM — Discrepancy Resolution & Orography Grid Consistency
--------------------------------------------------------------
1. Cause of the Three Orography Values:
   - Cell bounds: The Western Ghats escarpment cell containing Indabettu and Halagadaka Estate spans
     lat [13.00, 13.25]°N and lon [75.25, 75.50]°E (cell centre: 13.125°N, 75.375°E).
   - Coarse SRTM elevation: Exactly 658.4 m (658.4112 m in GEE reduceResolution; inspect_grid_registration.py:23).
   - In BH, the reported ERA5 orography of 812.1 m was the value at the north-eastern node (13.25°N, 75.50°E),
     selected because np.argmin on grid lines broke ties toward the higher coordinate.
   - In BC, Indabettu was evaluated against the south-western node (13.00°N, 75.25°E, ERA5=310.2 m),
     giving dz_ERA5 = 126.7 - 310.2 = -183.5 m (not -584.2 m, which was an informal transcription of another station).
   - The actual ERA5 orography at the cell's containing grid points spans 310.2 m (SW coastal plain) to 812.1 m (NE plateau crest).
2. Carry-Over in BC Positive Table:
   - The positive table in Section BC was partially carried over from AT's SRTM table, rather than sorted from dz_era5_arr.
   - Actual ERA5 orography, array indices, and true dz_ERA5 for the eight villages:
     * Torane (MH, code 9058): [i=0, j=1] (17.50°N, 73.75°E), ERA5 = 592.3 m, true dz_ERA5 = +374.9 m, dT = -2.44 °C.
     * Samse (KA, code 22013): [i=17, j=7] (13.25°N, 75.25°E), ERA5 = 528.6 m, true dz_ERA5 = +563.3 m, dT = -3.66 °C.
