ITEM BW — Final Restatement of the Product Claim
------------------------------------------------
Across 16,943 villages, 8.28% (1,403 villages) require a physical lapse-rate correction exceeding ±150 m (~1.0 °C) against ERA5 model orography—4.37% (741 villages) requiring cooling adjustments up to −4.16 °C (Dattathreyapeeta, KA, +640.5 m) and 3.91% (662 villages) requiring warming adjustments up to +3.37 °C (Nagave, MH, −519.0 m)—with a single 0.25° forecast cell at Charmadi Ghat containing 30 settlements spanning 1,108.8 m of relief that require bidirectional corrections of −2.75 °C to +3.01 °C; whereas subgrid topography alone exhibits a net warming asymmetry (559 warming vs 425 cooling) due to valley settlement siting, numerical model smoothing systematically depresses mountain ridges (by +25.5 m in high-relief cells), reversing the balance so that cooling corrections predominate in the operational forecast.


